{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CJQ2TVXSZVsMNz6qbqymbw","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tnarrative_guidance: 'CED 作为方法创新的叙事不成立，必须 reframe。新 angle：\"Why does online RL catastrophically\n2\t  fail for structured IE, and what works instead?\"——将 GRPO 全线失败升级为核心 contribution，RSFT\n3\t  作为 \"what works\" 的解法存在但不再强调 CED 独特性。EDCR 升级为独立 contribution。仍冲 EMNLP Main analysis\n4\t  track。\n5\t\n6\t  '\n7\timagined_experiments:\n8\t- name: CED vs flat-NLI RSFT ablation\n9\t  plan_id: plan_001\n10\t  description: '用 flat-NLI scoring 筛选 RSFT 训练数据，与 CED scoring 做 head-to-head 对比。 复用已有\n11\t    candidates，仅替换打分函数为 p_pos（无 contrastive margin）。\n12\t\n13\t    '\n14\t  expected_results:\n15\t    flatnli_rsft_rel_f1: 0.452\n16\t    flatnli_rsft_evi_f1: 0.8105\n17\t    flatnli_rsft_edcr: 0.662\n18\t    flatnli_rsft_selected_samples: 2850\n19\t    ced_rsft_best_rel_f1: 0.4655\n20\t    ced_rsft_best_evi_f1: 0.8087\n21\t    ced_rsft_best_edcr: 0.635\n22\t    ced_vs_flatnli_rel_f1_gap: 0.0135\n23\t    ced_vs_flatnli_evi_f1_gap: -0.0018\n24\t    ced_vs_flatnli_edcr_gap: -0.027\n25\t    paired_bootstrap_p_evi_f1: 0.38\n26\t    paired_bootstrap_p_edcr: 0.12\n27\t  result_rationale: '在 worst 档下，flat-NLI 的 p_pos 阈值筛选出的候选与 CED margin 筛选出的候选高度重叠 （Jaccard\n28\t    ~0.75）。原因：DocRED 中 entity-sharing distractor 的 NLI 分数分布与 gold evidence 有足够间距（MVP-1\n29\t    mean_margin=0.48），使得即使不做 contrastive 对比， 单纯高 p_pos 阈值也能过滤掉大部分 distractor。CED 的\n30\t    margin 机制在\"容易\"的 distractor 上无额外区分力，仅在 hard negative（p_neg > 0.6 的 distractor）上有优势，但这类样本\n31\t    占比 <15%。结果：evi_f1 gap 仅 -0.18pp（CED 甚至略低，因 margin 过滤过于严格导致 训练数据略少），EDCR gap -2.7pp\n32\t    方向正确但 p=0.12 不显著。Claim 2 核心假设—— \"CED 的对比性 margin 提供额外信息\"——统计上不成立。\n33\t\n34\t    '\n35\t  tables:\n36\t  - name: 'Table: CED vs flat-NLI RSFT Head-to-Head (Dev Set)'\n37\t    rows:\n38\t    - config: SFT baseline\n39\t      rel_f1: 0.4057\n40\t      evi_f1: 0.7979\n41\t      edcr: 0.7118\n42\t    - config: RSFT flat-NLI (best)\n43\t      rel_f1: 0.452\n44\t      evi_f1: 0.8105\n45\t      edcr: 0.662\n46\t    - config: RSFT CED r1 (s42)\n47\t      rel_f1: 0.4449\n48\t      evi_f1: 0.8187\n49\t      edcr: 0.6565\n50\t    - config: RSFT CED r1 (s44)\n51\t      rel_f1: 0.4655\n52\t      evi_f1: 0.8087\n53\t      edcr: 0.635\n54\t    - config: Δ (CED best − flat-NLI)\n55\t      rel_f1: +1.35pp\n56\t      evi_f1: −0.18pp\n57\t      edcr: −2.70pp\n58\t    - config: p-value (paired bootstrap)\n59\t      rel_f1: '0.08'\n60\t      evi_f1: '0.38'\n61\t      edcr: '0.12'\n62\t  figures_description:\n63\t  - 'Scatter plot: per-document Evi-F1 差异 (CED − flat-NLI)，大部分文档集中在 ±0.02 区间，仅少数 hard-negative-heavy\n64\t    文档 CED 明显优于 flat-NLI'\n65\t  analysis: 'CED 与 flat-NLI 无统计显著差异。CED 的 contrastive margin 仅在 hard negative 密集的\n66\t    文档子集上有边际优势，但全局来看两种 scoring 等价。这意味着 RSFT 的收益主要来自 rejection sampling 本身（过滤低质量候选），而非\n67\t    CED 特有的对比信号。Claim 2 需要 降级为 negative result 或合并到方法 ablation 中。\n68\t\n69\t    '\n70\t- name: Test set evaluation\n71\t  plan_id: plan_002\n72\t  description: '用 RSFT best config (s44) 在 DocRED test set 上评估，提交 CodaLab 获取官方 F1，\n73\t    本地计算 Evi-F1 和 EDCR。\n74\t\n75\t    '\n76\t  expected_results:\n77\t    test_rel_f1: 0.392\n78\t    test_ign_f1: 0.385\n79\t    test_evi_f1: 0.765\n80\t    test_edcr: 0.685\n81\t    test_precision: 0.398\n82\t    test_recall: 0.3865\n83\t    dev_to_test_rel_f1_drop: -0.0735\n84\t    dev_to_test_evi_f1_drop: -0.0437\n85\t    sft_test_rel_f1: 0.355\n86\t    sft_test_evi_f1: 0.752\n87\t    rsft_over_sft_test_rel_f1_gap: 0.037\n88\t    rsft_over_sft_test_evi_f1_gap: 0.013\n89\t  result_rationale: 'Dev→test 严重衰减是 worst 档的核心假设。DocRED test set 的标注分布与 dev set 存在\n90\t    已知偏移（test set annotator 更保守，relation 密度更低，evidence 链更短）。RSFT 在 dev set 上的优势部分来自对\n91\t    dev set 分布的过拟合——训练数据生成和 CED 打分均在 dev set 文档的 train split 上进行，候选筛选隐式适应了 train/dev\n92\t    的共享分布特征。Test set 的 unseen annotator 风格导致 rel_f1 从 0.4655 降至 0.3920（-7.35pp），evi_f1\n93\t    从 0.8087 降至 0.7650（-4.37pp）。EDCR 从 0.635 升至 0.685，因 test set 的 entity 分布更密集，distractor\n94\t    句子更多。rel_f1 仍高于 SFT baseline（+3.7pp），但绝对值 远低于 dev set 表现。evi_f1 0.765 虽仍远超 DREEAM\n95\t    的 57.34，但这个对比因评估 协议差异（生成式 vs attention-based）可能被 reviewer 质疑。\n96\t\n97\t    '\n98\t  tables:\n99\t  - name: 'Table: Dev vs Test Set Performance (RSFT s44)'\n100\t    rows:\n101\t    - split: Dev\n102\t      rel_f1: 0.4655\n103\t      evi_f1: 0.8087\n104\t      edcr: 0.635\n105\t    - split: Test\n106\t      rel_f1: 0.392\n107\t      evi_f1: 0.765\n108\t      edcr: 0.685\n109\t    - split: Δ (test − dev)\n110\t      rel_f1: −7.35pp\n111\t      evi_f1: −4.37pp\n112\t      edcr: +5.00pp\n113\t  - name: 'Table: Test Set Comparison (SFT vs RSFT)'\n114\t    rows:\n115\t    - method: SFT baseline\n116\t      rel_f1: 0.355\n117\t      evi_f1: 0.752\n118\t      edcr: 0.728\n119\t    - method: RSFT+CED (s44)\n120\t      rel_f1: 0.392\n121\t      evi_f1: 0.765\n122\t      edcr: 0.685\n123\t  figures_description:\n124\t  - 'Bar chart: Dev vs Test performance drop per metric，突出 rel_f1 的 15.8% 相对衰减'\n125\t  analysis: 'Test set 上 RSFT 仍优于 SFT，但 margin 缩窄。rel_f1 的相对衰减率 15.8% 高于典型 DocRE 方法（ATLOP\n126\t    约 5-8%），暗示 RSFT 对 dev set 分布有一定过拟合。EDCR 在 test set 上恶化，说明 test set 文档的 entity\n127\t    共现密度更高，distractor 问题更严重。 Publishability threshold 的必要条件（Evi-F1 > 57.34）仍满足，但 reviewer\n128\t    可能 质疑跨评估协议的可比性。\n129\t\n130\t    '\n131\t- name: EDCR pipeline 验证 + cross-method diagnostic table\n132\t  plan_id: plan_003\n133\t  description: '在所有 evidence-producing 方法上计算 EDCR，验证 EDCR 作为独立诊断指标的能力。\n134\t\n135\t    '\n136\t  expected_results:\n137\t    sft_edcr: 0.7118\n138\t    rsft_ced_best_edcr: 0.635\n139\t    rsft_flatnli_edcr: 0.662\n140\t    reranker_edcr: 0.665\n141\t    grpo_best_edcr: 0.8584\n142\t    ced_vs_flatnli_edcr_gap: -0.027\n143\t    edcr_evi_f1_correlation: -0.42\n144\t  result_rationale: '在 worst 档下，EDCR 的 cross-method 诊断能力被削弱。CED RSFT 与 flat-NLI RSFT\n145\t    的 EDCR 差异仅 2.7pp（方向正确但不显著），说明 CED 对 distractor 的过滤优势有限。 Reranker 的 EDCR（0.665）与\n146\t    RSFT flat-NLI 接近，因推理时 CED 重排仅能在 SFT 已生成的候选中选择，而 SFT 候选本身就包含大量 distractor。EDCR\n147\t    与 Evi-F1 的负相关 只有 r=-0.42（弱到中等），无法有力论证 \"Evi-F1 的盲区\"——部分高 EDCR 样本的 Evi-F1 也不高，两个指标部分重叠。EDCR\n148\t    作为独立 contribution 仍有价值（提出新维度），但 \"CED 改善 EDCR\" 的方法论故事很弱。\n149\t\n150\t    '\n151\t  tables:\n152\t  - name: 'Table: Cross-Method EDCR Diagnostic'\n153\t    rows:\n154\t    - method: GRPO+CED (ckpt-90)\n155\t      evi_f1: 0.5666\n156\t      edcr: 0.8584\n157\t      note: catastrophic forgetting\n158\t    - method: SFT baseline\n159\t      evi_f1: 0.7979\n160\t      edcr: 0.7118\n161\t      note: —\n162\t    - method: RSFT flat-NLI\n163\t      evi_f1: 0.8105\n164\t      edcr: 0.662\n165\t      note: —\n166\t    - method: CED-as-reranker\n167\t      evi_f1: 0.801\n168\t      edcr: 0.665\n169\t      note: inference-time only\n170\t    - method: RSFT+CED (s44)\n171\t      evi_f1: 0.8087\n172\t      edcr: 0.635\n173\t      note: best EDCR\n174\t  figures_description:\n175\t  - Evi-F1 vs EDCR scatter plot（per-document level），标注各方法的 centroid，展示两指标的弱负相关\n176\t  analysis: 'EDCR 作为诊断工具确实揭示了 Evi-F1 不能捕捉的 distractor citation 问题（GRPO 的 evi_f1=0.567\n177\t    但 EDCR=0.858 是极端案例）。但 CED 对 EDCR 的改善幅度有限（vs flat-NLI 仅 2.7pp），且 EDCR 绝对值仍然偏高（63.5%\n178\t    的被引证据仍是 distractor）， reviewer 可能质疑方法的实际影响力。Reframe: EDCR 的 contribution 在于指标设计\n179\t    本身，而非 CED 对 EDCR 的改善。\n180\t\n181\t    '\n182\t- name: DREEAM baseline reproduction\n183\t  plan_id: plan_004\n184\t  description: '在 DocRED dev set 上复现 DREEAM (RoBERTa-large) 的 Evi-F1，验证 57.34 是否可复现。\n185\t\n186\t    '\n187\t  expected_results:\n188\t    dreeam_dev_evi_f1_reproduced: 0.608\n189\t    dreeam_dev_rel_f1_reproduced: 0.632\n190\t    dreeam_paper_evi_f1: 0.5734\n191\t    dreeam_paper_rel_f1: 0.63\n192\t    reproduction_evi_f1_gap: 0.0346\n193\t    sais_dev_evi_f1_reproduced: 0.578\n194\t  result_rationale: 'DREEAM 论文报告的 57.34 是 test set Evi-F1，非 dev set。在 worst 档下，dev\n195\t    set 复现值为 60.8，显著高于论文 test set 数字。这产生两个问题：(1) 我们的 RSFT dev Evi-F1 80.87 与 DREEAM\n196\t    dev 60.8 的对比仍然成立（+20pp），但这是跨评估协议对比 （生成式句子索引 vs attention-based sentence extraction），reviewer\n197\t    可能质疑 apple-to-orange；(2) 如果 DREEAM dev 60.8 但 test 57.34，说明 encoder 方法也有 dev→test\n198\t    衰减，但我们的衰减幅度更大（-4.37pp vs -3.46pp），暗示生成式方法对 数据分布更敏感。更关键的是，复现值高于报告值会让 reviewer 质疑我们的评估\n199\t    pipeline 是否与 DREEAM 完全可比——可能存在句子分割、证据匹配阈值等微妙差异。\n200\t\n201\t    '\n202\t  tables:\n203\t  - name: 'Table: DREEAM/SAIS Reproduction vs Reported'\n204\t    rows:\n205\t    - method: DREEAM (paper, test)\n206\t      rel_f1: 0.63\n207\t      evi_f1: 0.5734\n208\t    - method: DREEAM (reproduced, dev)\n209\t      rel_f1: 0.632\n210\t      evi_f1: 0.608\n211\t    - method: SAIS (reproduced, dev)\n212\t      rel_f1: 0.615\n213\t      evi_f1: 0.578\n214\t    - method: RSFT+CED (dev)\n215\t      rel_f1: 0.4655\n216\t      evi_f1: 0.8087\n217\t  figures_description: []\n218\t  analysis: '复现值与报告值的偏差（+3.46pp）引入评估可比性疑虑。必须在论文中详细说明评估协议 差异（evidence 粒度、匹配方式），并承认跨范式对比的局限性。这削弱了\n219\t    Claim 1 中 \"超越 DREEAM\" 的叙事力度，但不致命——20pp 的 dev set 优势即使打折仍然 substantial。\n220\t\n221\t    '\n222\t- name: CED-as-reranker\n223\t  plan_id: plan_005\n224\t  description: '推理时用 CED 对 SFT 生成的 N=8 候选重排选最佳，无需额外训练。\n225\t\n226\t    '\n227\t  expected_results:\n228\t    reranker_rel_f1: 0.415\n229\t    reranker_evi_f1: 0.801\n230\t    reranker_edcr: 0.665\n231\t    sft_baseline_rel_f1: 0.4057\n232\t    sft_baseline_evi_f1: 0.7979\n233\t    sft_baseline_edcr: 0.7118\n234\t    reranker_over_sft_rel_f1: 0.0093\n235\t    reranker_over_sft_evi_f1: 0.0031\n236\t    reranker_over_sft_edcr: -0.0468\n237\t    reranker_inference_time_multiplier: 8.5\n238\t  result_rationale: '在 worst 档下，reranker 的 EDCR 改善有限（-4.68pp vs SFT）且远不及 RSFT（-7.68pp）。\n239\t    原因：CED 重排只能在 SFT 已生成的 8 个候选中选择，而 SFT 候选的 evidence 分布本身 就偏向 distractor——8 个候选中\n240\t    \"低 EDCR\" 的候选可能根本不存在（SFT 的 systematic bias 使所有候选都引用类似的 distractor 句子）。Rel_f1 微升（+0.93pp）因为\n241\t    CED 兼顾了 evidence 质量和抽取质量的联合打分，但提升幅度小。推理时间 8.5x（每个候选 都需要 NLI 推理）是实际部署的障碍。Reranker\n242\t    作为 \"training-free baseline\" 有方法论 价值，但在 worst 档下不构成独立 contribution。\n243\t\n244\t    '\n245\t  tables:\n246\t  - name: 'Table: CED-as-Reranker vs SFT vs RSFT (Dev Set)'\n247\t    rows:\n248\t    - method: SFT baseline\n249\t      rel_f1: 0.4057\n250\t      evi_f1: 0.7979\n251\t      edcr: 0.7118\n252\t      extra_train: 'No'\n253\t    - method: CED-as-reranker (N=8)\n254\t      rel_f1: 0.415\n255\t      evi_f1: 0.801\n256\t      edcr: 0.665\n257\t      extra_train: 'No'\n258\t    - method: RSFT+CED (s44)\n259\t      rel_f1: 0.4655\n260\t      evi_f1: 0.8087\n261\t      edcr: 0.635\n262\t      extra_train: 'Yes'\n263\t  figures_description:\n264\t  - EDCR 分布直方图：SFT 8 候选的 EDCR 分布，展示 reranker 的 selection ceiling——最优候选的 EDCR 仍然偏高\n265\t  analysis: 'Reranker 效果有限，印证 SFT 候选池本身的 distractor bias 是 bottleneck。RSFT 通过 改变模型权重从根源减少\n266\t    distractor 引用，reranker 只能在已有候选中做选择。在 worst 档下，reranker 降级为 ablation 中的一行数据，不再作为独立方法。\n267\t\n268\t    '\n269\t- name: Model size ablation (1.7B / 8B)\n270\t  plan_id: plan_006\n271\t  description: 'Qwen3-1.7B 和 Qwen3-8B 上复现 RSFT+CED pipeline，验证方法对模型规模的泛化性。\n272\t\n273\t    '\n274\t  expected_results:\n275\t    qwen3_1_7b_sft_rel_f1: 0.312\n276\t    qwen3_1_7b_sft_evi_f1: 0.735\n277\t    qwen3_1_7b_rsft_ced_rel_f1: 0.338\n278\t    qwen3_1_7b_rsft_ced_evi_f1: 0.752\n279\t    qwen3_1_7b_rsft_ced_edcr: 0.705\n280\t    qwen3_8b_sft_rel_f1: 0.458\n281\t    qwen3_8b_sft_evi_f1: 0.82\n282\t    qwen3_8b_rsft_ced_rel_f1: 0.475\n283\t    qwen3_8b_rsft_ced_evi_f1: 0.828\n284\t    qwen3_8b_rsft_ced_edcr: 0.648\n285\t    rsft_gain_1_7b_rel_f1: 0.026\n286\t    rsft_gain_4b_rel_f1: 0.0598\n287\t    rsft_gain_8b_rel_f1: 0.017\n288\t  result_rationale: '在 worst 档下，model size ablation 暴露 RSFT 收益的不稳定性。1.7B 模型的 SFT baseline\n289\t    较弱（rel_f1 0.312），RSFT 提升 +2.6pp——绝对收益小，因小模型生成候选 的质量上限低，CED 筛选后的训练数据量骤降（可能仅 ~1200\n290\t    samples vs 4B 的 2718）。 8B 模型的 SFT baseline 已较强（0.458），RSFT 仅提升 +1.7pp——边际递减，因强模型\n291\t    的 SFT 候选已经较好，CED 筛选的增量价值小。4B 是 sweet spot（+5.98pp），但这 可能是偶然而非系统性规律。EDCR 在 1.7B\n292\t    上改善最小（仅 -0.68pp vs SFT），进一步 削弱 CED 的方法论叙事。Reviewer 会指出 \"方法只在特定模型规模下有效\"。\n293\t\n294\t    '\n295\t  tables:\n296\t  - name: 'Table: Model Size Ablation (Dev Set)'\n297\t    rows:\n298\t    - model: Qwen3-1.7B SFT\n299\t      rel_f1: 0.312\n300\t      evi_f1: 0.735\n301\t      edcr: 0.72\n302\t    - model: Qwen3-1.7B RSFT+CED\n303\t      rel_f1: 0.338\n304\t      evi_f1: 0.752\n305\t      edcr: 0.705\n306\t    - model: Qwen3-4B SFT\n307\t      rel_f1: 0.4057\n308\t      evi_f1: 0.7979\n309\t      edcr: 0.7118\n310\t    - model: Qwen3-4B RSFT+CED\n311\t      rel_f1: 0.4655\n312\t      evi_f1: 0.8087\n313\t      edcr: 0.635\n314\t    - model: Qwen3-8B SFT\n315\t      rel_f1: 0.458\n316\t      evi_f1: 0.82\n317\t      edcr: 0.665\n318\t    - model: Qwen3-8B RSFT+CED\n319\t      rel_f1: 0.475\n320\t      evi_f1: 0.828\n321\t      edcr: 0.648\n322\t  figures_description:\n323\t  - '折线图: RSFT gain (Δrel_f1, Δevi_f1) vs model size，展示非单调关系——4B 是峰值'\n324\t  analysis: 'RSFT 收益对模型规模不鲁棒，4B 是 sweet spot 可能是 LoRA rank/lr 超参恰好匹配 而非方法论优势。在 reframed\n325\t    narrative 下，这个结果可以转化为 \"RSFT 的最优超参 与模型规模耦合\" 的 analysis contribution，但削弱了方法的通用性\n326\t    claim。\n327\t\n328\t    '\n329\t- name: Re-DocRED extension\n330\t  plan_id: plan_007\n331\t  description: '在 Re-DocRED（修正 false negative 标注）上评估 RSFT+CED，验证更干净标注下的表现。\n332\t\n333\t    '\n334\t  expected_results:\n335\t    redocred_sft_rel_f1: 0.525\n336\t    redocred_sft_evi_f1: 0.81\n337\t    redocred_rsft_ced_rel_f1: 0.548\n338\t    redocred_rsft_ced_evi_f1: 0.818\n339\t    redocred_rsft_ced_edcr: 0.592\n340\t    redocred_rsft_gain_rel_f1: 0.023\n341\t    redocred_rsft_gain_evi_f1: 0.008\n342\t  result_rationale: 'Re-DocRED 的标注更完整（修正了大量 false negative），SFT baseline 因更多 gold\n343\t    triples 而提升明显（rel_f1 0.525 vs DocRED 0.406）。但 RSFT 的增量收益缩小 （+2.3pp vs DocRED +5.98pp）。原因：Re-DocRED\n344\t    的更完整标注减少了 SFT 的 \"低悬果实\"，RSFT 的 rejection sampling 能筛选出的增量信号更少。EDCR 在 Re-DocRED\n345\t    上更低（0.592 vs DocRED 0.635），因更完整的 gold evidence 标注 使得之前被标为 distractor 的句子现在是 gold——CED\n346\t    的 false distractor 问题 在 Re-DocRED 上缓解。但这也意味着 CED 在 Re-DocRED 上的额外价值更小。\n347\t\n348\t    '\n349\t  tables:\n350\t  - name: 'Table: DocRED vs Re-DocRED (Dev Set)'\n351\t    rows:\n352\t    - dataset: DocRED SFT\n353\t      rel_f1: 0.4057\n354\t      evi_f1: 0.7979\n355\t      edcr: 0.7118\n356\t    - dataset: DocRED RSFT+CED\n357\t      rel_f1: 0.4655\n358\t      evi_f1: 0.8087\n359\t      edcr: 0.635\n360\t    - dataset: Re-DocRED SFT\n361\t      rel_f1: 0.525\n362\t      evi_f1: 0.81\n363\t      edcr: 0.635\n364\t    - dataset: Re-DocRED RSFT+CED\n365\t      rel_f1: 0.548\n366\t      evi_f1: 0.818\n367\t      edcr: 0.592\n368\t  figures_description: []\n369\t  analysis: 'Re-DocRED 上 RSFT 收益缩小是双刃剑：一方面 reviewer 会质疑方法在 clean data 上 的价值，另一方面可以论证\n370\t    \"RSFT+CED 在 noisy annotation 下价值更大\"——但这需要 与 reframed narrative（RL 失败分析）的主线协调。\n371\t\n372\t    '\n373\t- name: top_k ablation (k=1 vs k=3)\n374\t  plan_id: plan_008\n375\t  description: 'CED scoring 筛选 top_k=3（~8000 samples）vs top_k=1（~2718 samples）， 验证\n376\t    CED 过滤严格度对 RSFT 质量的影响。\n377\t\n378\t    '\n379\t  expected_results:\n380\t    topk1_selected_samples: 2718\n381\t    topk3_selected_samples: 8154\n382\t    topk1_mean_ced: 0.6683\n383\t    topk3_mean_ced: 0.512\n384\t    topk1_rsft_rel_f1: 0.4655\n385\t    topk1_rsft_evi_f1: 0.8087\n386\t    topk1_rsft_edcr: 0.635\n387\t    topk3_rsft_rel_f1: 0.458\n388\t    topk3_rsft_evi_f1: 0.805\n389\t    topk3_rsft_edcr: 0.672\n390\t    topk3_vs_topk1_rel_f1_gap: -0.0075\n391\t    topk3_vs_topk1_evi_f1_gap: -0.0037\n392\t    topk3_vs_topk1_edcr_gap: 0.037\n393\t  result_rationale: '在 worst 档下，top_k=3 的更多但更低质量训练数据导致轻微退化（rel_f1 -0.75pp， evi_f1\n394\t    -0.37pp，EDCR +3.7pp）。但退化幅度很小——说明 CED 分数在 top_k=1 到 top_k=3 区间内的质量差异不大（mean CED\n395\t    从 0.668 降至 0.512，但 floor 仍在 可接受范围）。这进一步支持 worst 档的核心论点：CED scoring 的精细程度不是 关键因素，rejection\n396\t    sampling 本身（而非 CED 特有的对比信号）驱动了收益。 Reviewer 可以用这个结果论证 \"随便什么 NLI 打分函数做 threshold\n397\t    filtering 都行\"。\n398\t\n399\t    '\n400\t  tables:\n401\t  - name: 'Table: top_k Ablation (Dev Set)'\n402\t    rows:\n403\t    - config: top_k=1 (2718 samples)\n404\t      rel_f1: 0.4655\n405\t      evi_f1: 0.8087\n406\t      edcr: 0.635\n407\t      mean_ced: 0.6683\n408\t    - config: top_k=3 (8154 samples)\n409\t      rel_f1: 0.458\n410\t      evi_f1: 0.805\n411\t      edcr: 0.672\n412\t      mean_ced: 0.512\n413\t  figures_description:\n414\t  - CED score 分布直方图：top_k=1 vs top_k=3 的 selected samples，展示 quality-quantity tradeoff\n415\t  analysis: 'top_k ablation 表明 CED 过滤的严格度影响有限，支撑 \"rejection sampling 本身 是关键\" 的叙事。在\n416\t    worst 档 reframe 中，这个结果可以纳入 \"what works\" 的 practical guideline 部分。\n417\t\n418\t    '\n419\t- name: GRPO forgetting 详细分析 + 可视化\n420\t  plan_id: plan_009\n421\t  description: '整理全部 GRPO checkpoint 轨迹，绘制 forgetting dynamics 可视化，支撑 Claim 3。\n422\t\n423\t    '\n424\t  expected_results:\n425\t    grpo_ced_kl001_trajectory:\n426\t      step_10:\n427\t        rel_f1: 0.003\n428\t        evi_f1: 0.72\n429\t        reward: 0.85\n430\t      step_20:\n431\t        rel_f1: 0.009\n432\t        evi_f1: 0.423\n433\t        reward: 0.92\n434\t      step_30:\n435\t        rel_f1: 0.034\n436\t        evi_f1: 0.589\n437\t        reward: 1.05\n438\t      step_50:\n439\t        rel_f1: 0.156\n440\t        evi_f1: 0.564\n441\t        reward: 1.18\n442\t      step_60:\n443\t        rel_f1: 0.147\n444\t        evi_f1: 0.576\n445\t        reward: 1.22\n446\t      step_90:\n447\t        rel_f1: 0.211\n448\t        evi_f1: 0.567\n449\t        reward: 1.37\n450\t      step_100:\n451\t        rel_f1: 0.217\n452\t        evi_f1: 0.575\n453\t        reward: 1.2\n454\t    grpo_lr5e6_trajectory:\n455\t      step_20:\n456\t        rel_f1: 0.008\n457\t        evi_f1: 0.628\n458\t        reward: 0.6\n459\t      step_40:\n460\t        rel_f1: 0.007\n461\t        evi_f1: 0.758\n462\t        reward: 0.75\n463\t      step_60:\n464\t        rel_f1: 0.009\n465\t        evi_f1: 0.81\n466\t        reward: 0.88\n467\t      step_80:\n468\t        rel_f1: 0.012\n469\t        evi_f1: 0.828\n470\t        reward: 0.95\n471\t      step_100:\n472\t        rel_f1: 0.014\n473\t        evi_f1: 0.85\n474\t        reward: 1.02\n475\t    flatnli_collapse_step: 25\n476\t    extract_only_collapse_step: 30\n477\t    forgetting_onset_step_range:\n478\t    - 5\n479\t    - 15\n480\t    reward_at_rel_f1_peak: 0.85\n481\t    reward_at_rel_f1_nadir: 1.37\n482\t  result_rationale: 'GRPO 数据已完整（registry 中多个 GRPO 实验），此 plan 主要是整理和可视化。 在 worst 档下，GRPO\n483\t    forgetting 分析被升级为核心 contribution。关键发现： (1) reward ↑ 但 rel_f1 ↓ 的 divergence 从\n484\t    step 5-15 开始，远早于收敛； (2) lr=5e-6 的慢速训练中 evi_f1 持续上升至 0.85（超过 SFT 的 0.798），但 rel_f1\n485\t    始终 <0.02——模型学会了生成好的 evidence 但完全丧失了 relation 抽取能力； (3) flat-NLI reward 在 step\n486\t    25 即 collapse（frac_zero_std=0.9），比 CED 更脆弱；(4) 这是 structured IE 场景下 catastrophic\n487\t    forgetting 的首个系统性 实证。连接 LongRLVR (ICLR 2026) 的 evidence grounding 梯度消失理论： GRPO\n488\t    的 group-relative advantage 在 structured output 空间中退化，因为 同一 prompt 的多个 rollout\n489\t    的结构化差异（relation 类型、数量）太大， advantage 估计噪声极高。\n490\t\n491\t    '\n492\t  tables:\n493\t  - name: 'Table: GRPO Forgetting Summary (All Reward Types)'\n494\t    rows:\n495\t    - reward: CED (lr=5e-5, KL=0.01)\n496\t      best_rel_f1: 0.217\n497\t      best_evi_f1: 0.575\n498\t      best_reward: 1.37\n499\t      collapse_step: N/A (slow decay)\n500\t    - reward: CED (lr=5e-6)\n501\t      best_rel_f1: 0.014\n502\t      best_evi_f1: 0.85\n503\t      best_reward: 1.02\n504\t      collapse_step: N/A (never recovers)\n505\t    - reward: flat-NLI\n506\t      best_rel_f1: ~0\n507\t      best_evi_f1: ~0\n508\t      best_reward: 0.293\n509\t      collapse_step: 25\n510\t    - reward: extract-only\n511\t      best_rel_f1: ~0\n512\t      best_evi_f1: ~0\n513\t      best_reward: ~0\n514\t      collapse_step: 30\n515\t  figures_description:\n516\t  - 'Figure 1: Reward-Task Divergence Curves——4-panel plot (一行两列 × 两行)，每 panel 一个\n517\t    reward type，x轴 training step，左 y轴 reward (blue)，右 y轴 rel_f1 (red dashed)，展示 reward\n518\t    ↑ + rel_f1 ↓ 的 scissors pattern'\n519\t  - 'Figure 2: Evidence-Extraction Tradeoff——lr=5e-6 的 evi_f1 vs rel_f1 trajectory，展示\n520\t    evi_f1 持续上升至 0.85 而 rel_f1 始终 <0.02 的极端 decoupling'\n521\t  - 'Figure 3: Forgetting Onset Heatmap——x轴 reward type，y轴 learning rate，cell 值为 rel_f1\n522\t    首次低于 SFT 50% 的 step number'\n523\t  analysis: '在 worst 档 reframe 下，这是论文最强 contribution。三个核心 insight： (1) GRPO 在 structured\n524\t    IE 上的失败不是超参问题——3 种 reward × 多个 lr 全线失败， 排除了 \"调参不够\" 的 reviewer 攻击； (2) evidence\n525\t    learning 和 relation extraction 在 GRPO 中 decouple——模型可以 学好 evidence（evi_f1 0.85\n526\t    > SFT 0.798）但完全丧失抽取能力，说明 GRPO 的梯度 被 evidence reward 主导，relation extraction 的离散结构化\n527\t    reward signal 被淹没； (3) 连接 LongRLVR 的理论，为 structured IE 场景提供首个实证验证。\n528\t\n529\t    '\n530\t- name: NLI model ablation (DeBERTa-base vs large)\n531\t  plan_id: plan_010\n532\t  description: 'DeBERTa-v3-base vs DeBERTa-v3-large 作为 CED scorer 的对比。\n533\t\n534\t    '\n535\t  expected_results:\n536\t    deberta_base_rsft_rel_f1: 0.4655\n537\t    deberta_base_rsft_evi_f1: 0.8087\n538\t    deberta_base_rsft_edcr: 0.635\n539\t    deberta_large_rsft_rel_f1: 0.459\n540\t    deberta_large_rsft_evi_f1: 0.812\n541\t    deberta_large_rsft_edcr: 0.641\n542\t    base_vs_large_evi_f1_gap: -0.0033\n543\t    base_vs_large_edcr_gap: -0.006\n544\t    deberta_large_mean_margin: 0.52\n545\t    deberta_base_mean_margin: 0.48\n546\t    deberta_large_discrimination_accuracy: 0.835\n547\t  result_rationale: '在 worst 档下，DeBERTa-large 的更强 NLI 能力（discrimination accuracy 83.5%\n548\t    vs base 81.5%）未转化为下游 RSFT 质量差异。原因：(1) CED 本身作为 scoring function 与 flat-NLI 无显著差异（plan_001\n549\t    结论），更强的 NLI 模型只是更精确地 计算了一个不产生额外价值的信号；(2) DeBERTa-large 的更大 margin（0.52 vs 0.48）\n550\t    导致筛选阈值变化，selected samples 略有不同但重叠度 >85%；(3) large 模型的 NLI 推理时间 ~3x base，cost-benefit\n551\t    不合理。结论：NLI 模型能力在 base 级别 已经足够，不是 bottleneck。\n552\t\n553\t    '\n554\t  tables:\n555\t  - name: 'Table: NLI Model Ablation'\n556\t    rows:\n557\t    - scorer: DeBERTa-v3-base\n558\t      mean_margin: 0.48\n559\t      disc_acc: 0.815\n560\t      rsft_evi_f1: 0.8087\n561\t      rsft_edcr: 0.635\n562\t    - scorer: DeBERTa-v3-large\n563\t      mean_margin: 0.52\n564\t      disc_acc: 0.835\n565\t      rsft_evi_f1: 0.812\n566\t      rsft_edcr: 0.641\n567\t  figures_description: []\n568\t  analysis: NLI 模型能力不是 bottleneck，与 plan_001 的结论一致：CED 的 scoring 精度（无论 来自对比机制还是更强\n569\t    NLI 模型）不是 RSFT 成功的关键因素。这个 negative result 在 reframed narrative 下可以简化为一句话：RSFT\n570\t    对 scoring function 的选择 不敏感，进一步支持 \"rejection sampling 本身是 what works\" 的论点。\n571\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"596c820e-21ec-4685-b435-a1fe07cb2330","uuid":"7f6233c1-f488-4ca3-a871-569f918a85df","timestamp":"2026-05-15T12:45:32.531Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0513_6/projects/faith-evidence-ie/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260515T120227/worst/review_context.yaml","content":"narrative_guidance: 'CED 作为方法创新的叙事不成立，必须 reframe。新 angle：\"Why does online RL catastrophically\n  fail for structured IE, and what works instead?\"——将 GRPO 全线失败升级为核心 contribution，RSFT\n  作为 \"what works\" 的解法存在但不再强调 CED 独特性。EDCR 升级为独立 contribution。仍冲 EMNLP Main analysis\n  track。\n\n  '\nimagined_experiments:\n- name: CED vs flat-NLI RSFT ablation\n  plan_id: plan_001\n  description: '用 flat-NLI scoring 筛选 RSFT 训练数据，与 CED scoring 做 head-to-head 对比。 复用已有\n    candidates，仅替换打分函数为 p_pos（无 contrastive margin）。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    flatnli_rsft_rel_f1: 0.452\n    flatnli_rsft_evi_f1: 0.8105\n    flatnli_rsft_edcr: 0.662\n    flatnli_rsft_selected_samples: 2850\n    ced_rsft_best_rel_f1: 0.4655\n    ced_rsft_best_evi_f1: 0.8087\n    ced_rsft_best_edcr: 0.635\n    ced_vs_flatnli_rel_f1_gap: 0.0135\n    ced_vs_flatnli_evi_f1_gap: -0.0018\n    ced_vs_flatnli_edcr_gap: -0.027\n    paired_bootstrap_p_evi_f1: 0.38\n    paired_bootstrap_p_edcr: 0.12\n  result_rationale: '在 worst 档下，flat-NLI 的 p_pos 阈值筛选出的候选与 CED margin 筛选出的候选高度重叠 （Jaccard\n    ~0.75）。原因：DocRED 中 entity-sharing distractor 的 NLI 分数分布与 gold evidence 有足够间距（MVP-1\n    mean_margin=0.48），使得即使不做 contrastive 对比， 单纯高 p_pos 阈值也能过滤掉大部分 distractor。CED 的\n    margin 机制在\"容易\"的 distractor 上无额外区分力，仅在 hard negative（p_neg > 0.6 的 distractor）上有优势，但这类样本\n    占比 <15%。结果：evi_f1 gap 仅 -0.18pp（CED 甚至略低，因 margin 过滤过于严格导致 训练数据略少），EDCR gap -2.7pp\n    方向正确但 p=0.12 不显著。Claim 2 核心假设—— \"CED 的对比性 margin 提供额外信息\"——统计上不成立。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: CED vs flat-NLI RSFT Head-to-Head (Dev Set)'\n    rows:\n    - config: SFT baseline\n      rel_f1: 0.4057\n      evi_f1: 0.7979\n      edcr: 0.7118\n    - config: RSFT flat-NLI (best)\n      rel_f1: 0.452\n      evi_f1: 0.8105\n      edcr: 0.662\n    - config: RSFT CED r1 (s42)\n      rel_f1: 0.4449\n      evi_f1: 0.8187\n      edcr: 0.6565\n    - config: RSFT CED r1 (s44)\n      rel_f1: 0.4655\n      evi_f1: 0.8087\n      edcr: 0.635\n    - config: Δ (CED best − flat-NLI)\n      rel_f1: +1.35pp\n      evi_f1: −0.18pp\n      edcr: −2.70pp\n    - config: p-value (paired bootstrap)\n      rel_f1: '0.08'\n      evi_f1: '0.38'\n      edcr: '0.12'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Scatter plot: per-document Evi-F1 差异 (CED − flat-NLI)，大部分文档集中在 ±0.02 区间，仅少数 hard-negative-heavy\n    文档 CED 明显优于 flat-NLI'\n  analysis: 'CED 与 flat-NLI 无统计显著差异。CED 的 contrastive margin 仅在 hard negative 密集的\n    文档子集上有边际优势，但全局来看两种 scoring 等价。这意味着 RSFT 的收益主要来自 rejection sampling 本身（过滤低质量候选），而非\n    CED 特有的对比信号。Claim 2 需要 降级为 negative result 或合并到方法 ablation 中。\n\n    '\n- name: Test set evaluation\n  plan_id: plan_002\n  description: '用 RSFT best config (s44) 在 DocRED test set 上评估，提交 CodaLab 获取官方 F1，\n    本地计算 Evi-F1 和 EDCR。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    test_rel_f1: 0.392\n    test_ign_f1: 0.385\n    test_evi_f1: 0.765\n    test_edcr: 0.685\n    test_precision: 0.398\n    test_recall: 0.3865\n    dev_to_test_rel_f1_drop: -0.0735\n    dev_to_test_evi_f1_drop: -0.0437\n    sft_test_rel_f1: 0.355\n    sft_test_evi_f1: 0.752\n    rsft_over_sft_test_rel_f1_gap: 0.037\n    rsft_over_sft_test_evi_f1_gap: 0.013\n  result_rationale: 'Dev→test 严重衰减是 worst 档的核心假设。DocRED test set 的标注分布与 dev set 存在\n    已知偏移（test set annotator 更保守，relation 密度更低，evidence 链更短）。RSFT 在 dev set 上的优势部分来自对\n    dev set 分布的过拟合——训练数据生成和 CED 打分均在 dev set 文档的 train split 上进行，候选筛选隐式适应了 train/dev\n    的共享分布特征。Test set 的 unseen annotator 风格导致 rel_f1 从 0.4655 降至 0.3920（-7.35pp），evi_f1\n    从 0.8087 降至 0.7650（-4.37pp）。EDCR 从 0.635 升至 0.685，因 test set 的 entity 分布更密集，distractor\n    句子更多。rel_f1 仍高于 SFT baseline（+3.7pp），但绝对值 远低于 dev set 表现。evi_f1 0.765 虽仍远超 DREEAM\n    的 57.34，但这个对比因评估 协议差异（生成式 vs attention-based）可能被 reviewer 质疑。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: Dev vs Test Set Performance (RSFT s44)'\n    rows:\n    - split: Dev\n      rel_f1: 0.4655\n      evi_f1: 0.8087\n      edcr: 0.635\n    - split: Test\n      rel_f1: 0.392\n      evi_f1: 0.765\n      edcr: 0.685\n    - split: Δ (test − dev)\n      rel_f1: −7.35pp\n      evi_f1: −4.37pp\n      edcr: +5.00pp\n  - name: 'Table: Test Set Comparison (SFT vs RSFT)'\n    rows:\n    - method: SFT baseline\n      rel_f1: 0.355\n      evi_f1: 0.752\n      edcr: 0.728\n    - method: RSFT+CED (s44)\n      rel_f1: 0.392\n      evi_f1: 0.765\n      edcr: 0.685\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Bar chart: Dev vs Test performance drop per metric，突出 rel_f1 的 15.8% 相对衰减'\n  analysis: 'Test set 上 RSFT 仍优于 SFT，但 margin 缩窄。rel_f1 的相对衰减率 15.8% 高于典型 DocRE 方法（ATLOP\n    约 5-8%），暗示 RSFT 对 dev set 分布有一定过拟合。EDCR 在 test set 上恶化，说明 test set 文档的 entity\n    共现密度更高，distractor 问题更严重。 Publishability threshold 的必要条件（Evi-F1 > 57.34）仍满足，但 reviewer\n    可能 质疑跨评估协议的可比性。\n\n    '\n- name: EDCR pipeline 验证 + cross-method diagnostic table\n  plan_id: plan_003\n  description: '在所有 evidence-producing 方法上计算 EDCR，验证 EDCR 作为独立诊断指标的能力。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    sft_edcr: 0.7118\n    rsft_ced_best_edcr: 0.635\n    rsft_flatnli_edcr: 0.662\n    reranker_edcr: 0.665\n    grpo_best_edcr: 0.8584\n    ced_vs_flatnli_edcr_gap: -0.027\n    edcr_evi_f1_correlation: -0.42\n  result_rationale: '在 worst 档下，EDCR 的 cross-method 诊断能力被削弱。CED RSFT 与 flat-NLI RSFT\n    的 EDCR 差异仅 2.7pp（方向正确但不显著），说明 CED 对 distractor 的过滤优势有限。 Reranker 的 EDCR（0.665）与\n    RSFT flat-NLI 接近，因推理时 CED 重排仅能在 SFT 已生成的候选中选择，而 SFT 候选本身就包含大量 distractor。EDCR\n    与 Evi-F1 的负相关 只有 r=-0.42（弱到中等），无法有力论证 \"Evi-F1 的盲区\"——部分高 EDCR 样本的 Evi-F1 也不高，两个指标部分重叠。EDCR\n    作为独立 contribution 仍有价值（提出新维度），但 \"CED 改善 EDCR\" 的方法论故事很弱。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: Cross-Method EDCR Diagnostic'\n    rows:\n    - method: GRPO+CED (ckpt-90)\n      evi_f1: 0.5666\n      edcr: 0.8584\n      note: catastrophic forgetting\n    - method: SFT baseline\n      evi_f1: 0.7979\n      edcr: 0.7118\n      note: —\n    - method: RSFT flat-NLI\n      evi_f1: 0.8105\n      edcr: 0.662\n      note: —\n    - method: CED-as-reranker\n      evi_f1: 0.801\n      edcr: 0.665\n      note: inference-time only\n    - method: RSFT+CED (s44)\n      evi_f1: 0.8087\n      edcr: 0.635\n      note: best EDCR\n  figures_description:\n  - Evi-F1 vs EDCR scatter plot（per-document level），标注各方法的 centroid，展示两指标的弱负相关\n  analysis: 'EDCR 作为诊断工具确实揭示了 Evi-F1 不能捕捉的 distractor citation 问题（GRPO 的 evi_f1=0.567\n    但 EDCR=0.858 是极端案例）。但 CED 对 EDCR 的改善幅度有限（vs flat-NLI 仅 2.7pp），且 EDCR 绝对值仍然偏高（63.5%\n    的被引证据仍是 distractor）， reviewer 可能质疑方法的实际影响力。Reframe: EDCR 的 contribution 在于指标设计\n    本身，而非 CED 对 EDCR 的改善。\n\n    '\n- name: DREEAM baseline reproduction\n  plan_id: plan_004\n  description: '在 DocRED dev set 上复现 DREEAM (RoBERTa-large) 的 Evi-F1，验证 57.34 是否可复现。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    dreeam_dev_evi_f1_reproduced: 0.608\n    dreeam_dev_rel_f1_reproduced: 0.632\n    dreeam_paper_evi_f1: 0.5734\n    dreeam_paper_rel_f1: 0.63\n    reproduction_evi_f1_gap: 0.0346\n    sais_dev_evi_f1_reproduced: 0.578\n  result_rationale: 'DREEAM 论文报告的 57.34 是 test set Evi-F1，非 dev set。在 worst 档下，dev\n    set 复现值为 60.8，显著高于论文 test set 数字。这产生两个问题：(1) 我们的 RSFT dev Evi-F1 80.87 与 DREEAM\n    dev 60.8 的对比仍然成立（+20pp），但这是跨评估协议对比 （生成式句子索引 vs attention-based sentence extraction），reviewer\n    可能质疑 apple-to-orange；(2) 如果 DREEAM dev 60.8 但 test 57.34，说明 encoder 方法也有 dev→test\n    衰减，但我们的衰减幅度更大（-4.37pp vs -3.46pp），暗示生成式方法对 数据分布更敏感。更关键的是，复现值高于报告值会让 reviewer 质疑我们的评估\n    pipeline 是否与 DREEAM 完全可比——可能存在句子分割、证据匹配阈值等微妙差异。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: DREEAM/SAIS Reproduction vs Reported'\n    rows:\n    - method: DREEAM (paper, test)\n      rel_f1: 0.63\n      evi_f1: 0.5734\n    - method: DREEAM (reproduced, dev)\n      rel_f1: 0.632\n      evi_f1: 0.608\n    - method: SAIS (reproduced, dev)\n      rel_f1: 0.615\n      evi_f1: 0.578\n    - method: RSFT+CED (dev)\n      rel_f1: 0.4655\n      evi_f1: 0.8087\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: '复现值与报告值的偏差（+3.46pp）引入评估可比性疑虑。必须在论文中详细说明评估协议 差异（evidence 粒度、匹配方式），并承认跨范式对比的局限性。这削弱了\n    Claim 1 中 \"超越 DREEAM\" 的叙事力度，但不致命——20pp 的 dev set 优势即使打折仍然 substantial。\n\n    '\n- name: CED-as-reranker\n  plan_id: plan_005\n  description: '推理时用 CED 对 SFT 生成的 N=8 候选重排选最佳，无需额外训练。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    reranker_rel_f1: 0.415\n    reranker_evi_f1: 0.801\n    reranker_edcr: 0.665\n    sft_baseline_rel_f1: 0.4057\n    sft_baseline_evi_f1: 0.7979\n    sft_baseline_edcr: 0.7118\n    reranker_over_sft_rel_f1: 0.0093\n    reranker_over_sft_evi_f1: 0.0031\n    reranker_over_sft_edcr: -0.0468\n    reranker_inference_time_multiplier: 8.5\n  result_rationale: '在 worst 档下，reranker 的 EDCR 改善有限（-4.68pp vs SFT）且远不及 RSFT（-7.68pp）。\n    原因：CED 重排只能在 SFT 已生成的 8 个候选中选择，而 SFT 候选的 evidence 分布本身 就偏向 distractor——8 个候选中\n    \"低 EDCR\" 的候选可能根本不存在（SFT 的 systematic bias 使所有候选都引用类似的 distractor 句子）。Rel_f1 微升（+0.93pp）因为\n    CED 兼顾了 evidence 质量和抽取质量的联合打分，但提升幅度小。推理时间 8.5x（每个候选 都需要 NLI 推理）是实际部署的障碍。Reranker\n    作为 \"training-free baseline\" 有方法论 价值，但在 worst 档下不构成独立 contribution。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: CED-as-Reranker vs SFT vs RSFT (Dev Set)'\n    rows:\n    - method: SFT baseline\n      rel_f1: 0.4057\n      evi_f1: 0.7979\n      edcr: 0.7118\n      extra_train: 'No'\n    - method: CED-as-reranker (N=8)\n      rel_f1: 0.415\n      evi_f1: 0.801\n      edcr: 0.665\n      extra_train: 'No'\n    - method: RSFT+CED (s44)\n      rel_f1: 0.4655\n      evi_f1: 0.8087\n      edcr: 0.635\n      extra_train: 'Yes'\n  figures_description:\n  - EDCR 分布直方图：SFT 8 候选的 EDCR 分布，展示 reranker 的 selection ceiling——最优候选的 EDCR 仍然偏高\n  analysis: 'Reranker 效果有限，印证 SFT 候选池本身的 distractor bias 是 bottleneck。RSFT 通过 改变模型权重从根源减少\n    distractor 引用，reranker 只能在已有候选中做选择。在 worst 档下，reranker 降级为 ablation 中的一行数据，不再作为独立方法。\n\n    '\n- name: Model size ablation (1.7B / 8B)\n  plan_id: plan_006\n  description: 'Qwen3-1.7B 和 Qwen3-8B 上复现 RSFT+CED pipeline，验证方法对模型规模的泛化性。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    qwen3_1_7b_sft_rel_f1: 0.312\n    qwen3_1_7b_sft_evi_f1: 0.735\n    qwen3_1_7b_rsft_ced_rel_f1: 0.338\n    qwen3_1_7b_rsft_ced_evi_f1: 0.752\n    qwen3_1_7b_rsft_ced_edcr: 0.705\n    qwen3_8b_sft_rel_f1: 0.458\n    qwen3_8b_sft_evi_f1: 0.82\n    qwen3_8b_rsft_ced_rel_f1: 0.475\n    qwen3_8b_rsft_ced_evi_f1: 0.828\n    qwen3_8b_rsft_ced_edcr: 0.648\n    rsft_gain_1_7b_rel_f1: 0.026\n    rsft_gain_4b_rel_f1: 0.0598\n    rsft_gain_8b_rel_f1: 0.017\n  result_rationale: '在 worst 档下，model size ablation 暴露 RSFT 收益的不稳定性。1.7B 模型的 SFT baseline\n    较弱（rel_f1 0.312），RSFT 提升 +2.6pp——绝对收益小，因小模型生成候选 的质量上限低，CED 筛选后的训练数据量骤降（可能仅 ~1200\n    samples vs 4B 的 2718）。 8B 模型的 SFT baseline 已较强（0.458），RSFT 仅提升 +1.7pp——边际递减，因强模型\n    的 SFT 候选已经较好，CED 筛选的增量价值小。4B 是 sweet spot（+5.98pp），但这 可能是偶然而非系统性规律。EDCR 在 1.7B\n    上改善最小（仅 -0.68pp vs SFT），进一步 削弱 CED 的方法论叙事。Reviewer 会指出 \"方法只在特定模型规模下有效\"。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: Model Size Ablation (Dev Set)'\n    rows:\n    - model: Qwen3-1.7B SFT\n      rel_f1: 0.312\n      evi_f1: 0.735\n      edcr: 0.72\n    - model: Qwen3-1.7B RSFT+CED\n      rel_f1: 0.338\n      evi_f1: 0.752\n      edcr: 0.705\n    - model: Qwen3-4B SFT\n      rel_f1: 0.4057\n      evi_f1: 0.7979\n      edcr: 0.7118\n    - model: Qwen3-4B RSFT+CED\n      rel_f1: 0.4655\n      evi_f1: 0.8087\n      edcr: 0.635\n    - model: Qwen3-8B SFT\n      rel_f1: 0.458\n      evi_f1: 0.82\n      edcr: 0.665\n    - model: Qwen3-8B RSFT+CED\n      rel_f1: 0.475\n      evi_f1: 0.828\n      edcr: 0.648\n  figures_description:\n  - '折线图: RSFT gain (Δrel_f1, Δevi_f1) vs model size，展示非单调关系——4B 是峰值'\n  analysis: 'RSFT 收益对模型规模不鲁棒，4B 是 sweet spot 可能是 LoRA rank/lr 超参恰好匹配 而非方法论优势。在 reframed\n    narrative 下，这个结果可以转化为 \"RSFT 的最优超参 与模型规模耦合\" 的 analysis contribution，但削弱了方法的通用性\n    claim。\n\n    '\n- name: Re-DocRED extension\n  plan_id: plan_007\n  description: '在 Re-DocRED（修正 false negative 标注）上评估 RSFT+CED，验证更干净标注下的表现。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    redocred_sft_rel_f1: 0.525\n    redocred_sft_evi_f1: 0.81\n    redocred_rsft_ced_rel_f1: 0.548\n    redocred_rsft_ced_evi_f1: 0.818\n    redocred_rsft_ced_edcr: 0.592\n    redocred_rsft_gain_rel_f1: 0.023\n    redocred_rsft_gain_evi_f1: 0.008\n  result_rationale: 'Re-DocRED 的标注更完整（修正了大量 false negative），SFT baseline 因更多 gold\n    triples 而提升明显（rel_f1 0.525 vs DocRED 0.406）。但 RSFT 的增量收益缩小 （+2.3pp vs DocRED +5.98pp）。原因：Re-DocRED\n    的更完整标注减少了 SFT 的 \"低悬果实\"，RSFT 的 rejection sampling 能筛选出的增量信号更少。EDCR 在 Re-DocRED\n    上更低（0.592 vs DocRED 0.635），因更完整的 gold evidence 标注 使得之前被标为 distractor 的句子现在是 gold——CED\n    的 false distractor 问题 在 Re-DocRED 上缓解。但这也意味着 CED 在 Re-DocRED 上的额外价值更小。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: DocRED vs Re-DocRED (Dev Set)'\n    rows:\n    - dataset: DocRED SFT\n      rel_f1: 0.4057\n      evi_f1: 0.7979\n      edcr: 0.7118\n    - dataset: DocRED RSFT+CED\n      rel_f1: 0.4655\n      evi_f1: 0.8087\n      edcr: 0.635\n    - dataset: Re-DocRED SFT\n      rel_f1: 0.525\n      evi_f1: 0.81\n      edcr: 0.635\n    - dataset: Re-DocRED RSFT+CED\n      rel_f1: 0.548\n      evi_f1: 0.818\n      edcr: 0.592\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: 'Re-DocRED 上 RSFT 收益缩小是双刃剑：一方面 reviewer 会质疑方法在 clean data 上 的价值，另一方面可以论证\n    \"RSFT+CED 在 noisy annotation 下价值更大\"——但这需要 与 reframed narrative（RL 失败分析）的主线协调。\n\n    '\n- name: top_k ablation (k=1 vs k=3)\n  plan_id: plan_008\n  description: 'CED scoring 筛选 top_k=3（~8000 samples）vs top_k=1（~2718 samples）， 验证\n    CED 过滤严格度对 RSFT 质量的影响。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    topk1_selected_samples: 2718\n    topk3_selected_samples: 8154\n    topk1_mean_ced: 0.6683\n    topk3_mean_ced: 0.512\n    topk1_rsft_rel_f1: 0.4655\n    topk1_rsft_evi_f1: 0.8087\n    topk1_rsft_edcr: 0.635\n    topk3_rsft_rel_f1: 0.458\n    topk3_rsft_evi_f1: 0.805\n    topk3_rsft_edcr: 0.672\n    topk3_vs_topk1_rel_f1_gap: -0.0075\n    topk3_vs_topk1_evi_f1_gap: -0.0037\n    topk3_vs_topk1_edcr_gap: 0.037\n  result_rationale: '在 worst 档下，top_k=3 的更多但更低质量训练数据导致轻微退化（rel_f1 -0.75pp， evi_f1\n    -0.37pp，EDCR +3.7pp）。但退化幅度很小——说明 CED 分数在 top_k=1 到 top_k=3 区间内的质量差异不大（mean CED\n    从 0.668 降至 0.512，但 floor 仍在 可接受范围）。这进一步支持 worst 档的核心论点：CED scoring 的精细程度不是 关键因素，rejection\n    sampling 本身（而非 CED 特有的对比信号）驱动了收益。 Reviewer 可以用这个结果论证 \"随便什么 NLI 打分函数做 threshold\n    filtering 都行\"。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: top_k Ablation (Dev Set)'\n    rows:\n    - config: top_k=1 (2718 samples)\n      rel_f1: 0.4655\n      evi_f1: 0.8087\n      edcr: 0.635\n      mean_ced: 0.6683\n    - config: top_k=3 (8154 samples)\n      rel_f1: 0.458\n      evi_f1: 0.805\n      edcr: 0.672\n      mean_ced: 0.512\n  figures_description:\n  - CED score 分布直方图：top_k=1 vs top_k=3 的 selected samples，展示 quality-quantity tradeoff\n  analysis: 'top_k ablation 表明 CED 过滤的严格度影响有限，支撑 \"rejection sampling 本身 是关键\" 的叙事。在\n    worst 档 reframe 中，这个结果可以纳入 \"what works\" 的 practical guideline 部分。\n\n    '\n- name: GRPO forgetting 详细分析 + 可视化\n  plan_id: plan_009\n  description: '整理全部 GRPO checkpoint 轨迹，绘制 forgetting dynamics 可视化，支撑 Claim 3。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    grpo_ced_kl001_trajectory:\n      step_10:\n        rel_f1: 0.003\n        evi_f1: 0.72\n        reward: 0.85\n      step_20:\n        rel_f1: 0.009\n        evi_f1: 0.423\n        reward: 0.92\n      step_30:\n        rel_f1: 0.034\n        evi_f1: 0.589\n        reward: 1.05\n      step_50:\n        rel_f1: 0.156\n        evi_f1: 0.564\n        reward: 1.18\n      step_60:\n        rel_f1: 0.147\n        evi_f1: 0.576\n        reward: 1.22\n      step_90:\n        rel_f1: 0.211\n        evi_f1: 0.567\n        reward: 1.37\n      step_100:\n        rel_f1: 0.217\n        evi_f1: 0.575\n        reward: 1.2\n    grpo_lr5e6_trajectory:\n      step_20:\n        rel_f1: 0.008\n        evi_f1: 0.628\n        reward: 0.6\n      step_40:\n        rel_f1: 0.007\n        evi_f1: 0.758\n        reward: 0.75\n      step_60:\n        rel_f1: 0.009\n        evi_f1: 0.81\n        reward: 0.88\n      step_80:\n        rel_f1: 0.012\n        evi_f1: 0.828\n        reward: 0.95\n      step_100:\n        rel_f1: 0.014\n        evi_f1: 0.85\n        reward: 1.02\n    flatnli_collapse_step: 25\n    extract_only_collapse_step: 30\n    forgetting_onset_step_range:\n    - 5\n    - 15\n    reward_at_rel_f1_peak: 0.85\n    reward_at_rel_f1_nadir: 1.37\n  result_rationale: 'GRPO 数据已完整（registry 中多个 GRPO 实验），此 plan 主要是整理和可视化。 在 worst 档下，GRPO\n    forgetting 分析被升级为核心 contribution。关键发现： (1) reward ↑ 但 rel_f1 ↓ 的 divergence 从\n    step 5-15 开始，远早于收敛； (2) lr=5e-6 的慢速训练中 evi_f1 持续上升至 0.85（超过 SFT 的 0.798），但 rel_f1\n    始终 <0.02——模型学会了生成好的 evidence 但完全丧失了 relation 抽取能力； (3) flat-NLI reward 在 step\n    25 即 collapse（frac_zero_std=0.9），比 CED 更脆弱；(4) 这是 structured IE 场景下 catastrophic\n    forgetting 的首个系统性 实证。连接 LongRLVR (ICLR 2026) 的 evidence grounding 梯度消失理论： GRPO\n    的 group-relative advantage 在 structured output 空间中退化，因为 同一 prompt 的多个 rollout\n    的结构化差异（relation 类型、数量）太大， advantage 估计噪声极高。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: GRPO Forgetting Summary (All Reward Types)'\n    rows:\n    - reward: CED (lr=5e-5, KL=0.01)\n      best_rel_f1: 0.217\n      best_evi_f1: 0.575\n      best_reward: 1.37\n      collapse_step: N/A (slow decay)\n    - reward: CED (lr=5e-6)\n      best_rel_f1: 0.014\n      best_evi_f1: 0.85\n      best_reward: 1.02\n      collapse_step: N/A (never recovers)\n    - reward: flat-NLI\n      best_rel_f1: ~0\n      best_evi_f1: ~0\n      best_reward: 0.293\n      collapse_step: 25\n    - reward: extract-only\n      best_rel_f1: ~0\n      best_evi_f1: ~0\n      best_reward: ~0\n      collapse_step: 30\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Figure 1: Reward-Task Divergence Curves——4-panel plot (一行两列 × 两行)，每 panel 一个\n    reward type，x轴 training step，左 y轴 reward (blue)，右 y轴 rel_f1 (red dashed)，展示 reward\n    ↑ + rel_f1 ↓ 的 scissors pattern'\n  - 'Figure 2: Evidence-Extraction Tradeoff——lr=5e-6 的 evi_f1 vs rel_f1 trajectory，展示\n    evi_f1 持续上升至 0.85 而 rel_f1 始终 <0.02 的极端 decoupling'\n  - 'Figure 3: Forgetting Onset Heatmap——x轴 reward type，y轴 learning rate，cell 值为 rel_f1\n    首次低于 SFT 50% 的 step number'\n  analysis: '在 worst 档 reframe 下，这是论文最强 contribution。三个核心 insight： (1) GRPO 在 structured\n    IE 上的失败不是超参问题——3 种 reward × 多个 lr 全线失败， 排除了 \"调参不够\" 的 reviewer 攻击； (2) evidence\n    learning 和 relation extraction 在 GRPO 中 decouple——模型可以 学好 evidence（evi_f1 0.85\n    > SFT 0.798）但完全丧失抽取能力，说明 GRPO 的梯度 被 evidence reward 主导，relation extraction 的离散结构化\n    reward signal 被淹没； (3) 连接 LongRLVR 的理论，为 structured IE 场景提供首个实证验证。\n\n    '\n- name: NLI model ablation (DeBERTa-base vs large)\n  plan_id: plan_010\n  description: 'DeBERTa-v3-base vs DeBERTa-v3-large 作为 CED scorer 的对比。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    deberta_base_rsft_rel_f1: 0.4655\n    deberta_base_rsft_evi_f1: 0.8087\n    deberta_base_rsft_edcr: 0.635\n    deberta_large_rsft_rel_f1: 0.459\n    deberta_large_rsft_evi_f1: 0.812\n    deberta_large_rsft_edcr: 0.641\n    base_vs_large_evi_f1_gap: -0.0033\n    base_vs_large_edcr_gap: -0.006\n    deberta_large_mean_margin: 0.52\n    deberta_base_mean_margin: 0.48\n    deberta_large_discrimination_accuracy: 0.835\n  result_rationale: '在 worst 档下，DeBERTa-large 的更强 NLI 能力（discrimination accuracy 83.5%\n    vs base 81.5%）未转化为下游 RSFT 质量差异。原因：(1) CED 本身作为 scoring function 与 flat-NLI 无显著差异（plan_001\n    结论），更强的 NLI 模型只是更精确地 计算了一个不产生额外价值的信号；(2) DeBERTa-large 的更大 margin（0.52 vs 0.48）\n    导致筛选阈值变化，selected samples 略有不同但重叠度 >85%；(3) large 模型的 NLI 推理时间 ~3x base，cost-benefit\n    不合理。结论：NLI 模型能力在 base 级别 已经足够，不是 bottleneck。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: NLI Model Ablation'\n    rows:\n    - scorer: DeBERTa-v3-base\n      mean_margin: 0.48\n      disc_acc: 0.815\n      rsft_evi_f1: 0.8087\n      rsft_edcr: 0.635\n    - scorer: DeBERTa-v3-large\n      mean_margin: 0.52\n      disc_acc: 0.835\n      rsft_evi_f1: 0.812\n      rsft_edcr: 0.641\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: NLI 模型能力不是 bottleneck，与 plan_001 的结论一致：CED 的 scoring 精度（无论 来自对比机制还是更强\n    NLI 模型）不是 RSFT 成功的关键因素。这个 negative result 在 reframed narrative 下可以简化为一句话：RSFT\n    对 scoring function 的选择 不敏感，进一步支持 \"rejection sampling 本身是 what works\" 的论点。\n","numLines":571,"startLine":1,"totalLines":571}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012YJWzA9fkf2cqKzHLW7oEd","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"EMNLP 2026 reviewer guidelines review form\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"FAQ - EMNLP 2026\",\"url\":\"https://2026.emnlp.org/faq/\"},{\"title\":\"LINGUIST List 37.972 Confs: 2026 Conference on Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing (Hungary)\",\"url\":\"https://linguistlist.org/issues/37/972/\"},{\"title\":\"EMNLP 2026 : The 2026 Conference on Empirical Methods in N\",\"url\":\"https://callforpaper.org/call-for-papers-emnlp-2026\"},{\"title\":\"EMNLP 2026 | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=EMNLP%2F2026\"},{\"title\":\"EMNLP | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=EMNLP\"},{\"title\":\"Authors Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/authors\"},{\"title\":\"ARR Reviewer Guidelines\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines\"},{\"title\":\"Changes to reviewer volunteering requirement and incentives in May 2025 cycle (EMNLP 2025)\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/incentives2025\"},{\"title\":\"EMNLP 2026 (@emnlpmeeting) / Posts / X\",\"url\":\"https://x.com/emnlpmeeting\"},{\"title\":\"EMNLP 2025 (@emnlpmeeting) · X\",\"url\":\"https://twitter.com/emnlpmeeting\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found relevant information about EMNLP 2026 and reviewer guidelines:\n\n## EMNLP 2026 Overview\n\nEMNLP 2026 will use ACL Rolling Review (ARR) as a reviewing system, but final decisions will be made by the conference. Both submissions of articles for review and commitment of reviewed articles to the conference will be performed via the Open Review platform, where authors submit articles to ARR to receive reviews and meta-reviews, then commit their reviewed articles to EMNLP 2026.\n\n## Key Deadlines\n\nIf you receive assignments, your reviews must be completed by July 6, or your meta-reviews by July 29.\n\n## Reviewer Guidelines\n\nFor EMNLP 2026, the conference follows ARR reviewer guidelines. To preserve the merits of double-blind review, reviewers for *ACL conferences should be instructed not to actively try to discover the identity of the authors and not to let any suspicion or knowledge of author identity affect their judgment of the paper.\n\nStarting in May 2025, ARR adopts a policy on 'highly irresponsible' (meta-)reviewers, where program chairs and ARR EiCs will consider egregious cases including extremely terse reviews, unprofessional tone, and LLM-generated reviews.\n\nThe specific EMNLP 2026 review form and detailed reviewer guidelines can be accessed through the OpenReview homepage for EMNLP 2026 and the ACL Rolling Review website at aclrollingreview.org.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"596c820e-21ec-4685-b435-a1fe07cb2330","uuid":"305dce3b-c46a-4d7f-99f7-75ee588e24f1","timestamp":"2026-05-15T12:45:36.340Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"EMNLP 2026 reviewer guidelines review form","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01UHP1rBkMjtXqh3uG1Sq6UD","content":[{"title":"FAQ - EMNLP 2026","url":"https://2026.emnlp.org/faq/"},{"title":"LINGUIST List 37.972 Confs: 2026 Conference on Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing (Hungary)","url":"https://linguistlist.org/issues/37/972/"},{"title":"EMNLP 2026 : The 2026 Conference on Empirical Methods in N","url":"https://callforpaper.org/call-for-papers-emnlp-2026"},{"title":"EMNLP 2026 | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=EMNLP%2F2026"},{"title":"EMNLP | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=EMNLP"},{"title":"Authors Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/authors"},{"title":"ARR Reviewer Guidelines","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines"},{"title":"Changes to reviewer volunteering requirement and incentives in May 2025 cycle (EMNLP 2025)","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/incentives2025"},{"title":"EMNLP 2026 (@emnlpmeeting) / Posts / X","url":"https://x.com/emnlpmeeting"},{"title":"EMNLP 2025 (@emnlpmeeting) · X","url":"https://twitter.com/emnlpmeeting"}]},"Based on the search results, I found relevant information about EMNLP 2026 and reviewer guidelines:\n\n## EMNLP 2026 Overview\n\nEMNLP 2026 will use ACL Rolling Review (ARR) as a reviewing system, but final decisions will be made by the conference. Both submissions of articles for review and commitment of reviewed articles to the conference will be performed via the Open Review platform, where authors submit articles to ARR to receive reviews and meta-reviews, then commit their reviewed articles to EMNLP 2026.\n\n## Key Deadlines\n\nIf you receive assignments, your reviews must be completed by July 6, or your meta-reviews by July 29.\n\n## Reviewer Guidelines\n\nFor EMNLP 2026, the conference follows ARR reviewer guidelines. To preserve the merits of double-blind review, reviewers for *ACL conferences should be instructed not to actively try to discover the identity of the authors and not to let any suspicion or knowledge of author identity affect their judgment of the paper.\n\nStarting in May 2025, ARR adopts a policy on 'highly irresponsible' (meta-)reviewers, where program chairs and ARR EiCs will consider egregious cases including extremely terse reviews, unprofessional tone, and LLM-generated reviews.\n\nThe specific EMNLP 2026 review form and detailed reviewer guidelines can be accessed through the OpenReview homepage for EMNLP 2026 and the ACL Rolling Review website at aclrollingreview.org."],"durationSeconds":7.205898394999998}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MCmJwtic8CWHi6vuDa5XKP","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"EMNLP 2025 reviewer guidelines review form scoring criteria\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"NAACL-HLT 2021 Instructions for Reviewers - EMNLP 2025\",\"url\":\"https://2025.emnlp.org/reviewer/instructions/\"},{\"title\":\"Changes to reviewer volunteering requirement and incentives in May 2025 cycle (EMNLP 2025)\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/incentives2025\"},{\"title\":\"Automatically Measuring Peer Review's Utility for Authors\",\"url\":\"https://aclanthology.org/2025.emnlp-main.1476.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"ICML 2025 Peer Review FAQ\",\"url\":\"https://icml.cc/Conferences/2025/PeerReviewFAQ\"},{\"title\":\"‭ACL Peer Review Committee Report‬\",\"url\":\"https://www.aclweb.org/adminwiki/images/d/d3/ACL_Peer_Review_Committee_Report2_Incentives_May_2025.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"[Policy Spotlight] EMNLP 2025 Criteria for “Highly Irresponsible” Reviewers — What It Means & Why It Matters | CSPaper Forum\",\"url\":\"https://forum.cspaper.org/topic/70/policy-spotlight-emnlp-2025-criteria-for-highly-irresponsible-reviewers-what-it-means-why-it-matters\"},{\"title\":\"[Policy Spotlight] EMNLP 2025 Criteria for “Highly Irresponsible” Reviewers — What It Means & Why It Matters | CSPaper\",\"url\":\"https://cspaper.org/topic/70/policy-spotlight-emnlp-2025-criteria-for-highly-irresponsible-reviewers-what-it-means-why-it-matters\"},{\"title\":\"EMNLP 2025 Conference | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=EMNLP%2F2025%2FConference\"},{\"title\":\"ACL Policies for Review and Citation - Admin Wiki\",\"url\":\"https://www.aclweb.org/adminwiki/index.php/ACL_Policies_for_Review_and_Citation\"},{\"title\":\"Authors Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/authors\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about EMNLP 2025 reviewer guidelines and scoring criteria:\n\n## Scoring Scale\n\nEMNLP 2025 uses a 5-point scale with half-point increments, similar to ACL 2020. The detailed explanation for each point level is provided in the review form.\n\nImportantly, a rating of 3 (ambivalent) is allowed, and reviewers are encouraged to take a stand on whether the paper is above or below the borderline by selecting 2.5 or 3.5, though if a paper is truly borderline or the reviewer cannot decide, a score of 3 should be used.\n\n## Review Form Structure\n\nThe review form consists of four main sections, with the first being an In-Depth Review section for providing overall assessment of the paper, which includes a core review that should describe the main contributions the paper intended to make and how well it succeeds.\n\n## Reproducibility Assessment\n\nEMNLP 2025 includes a reproducibility checklist, and reviewers answer questions about the paper's reproducibility using scores of 1-5. An \"N/A\" score may be used for papers that do not include empirical results.\n\n## Decision-Making Process\n\nDecisions are made not just on scores and certainly not on average scores, but also take into account the whole review, reviewer discussion, and Area Chair meta-reviews and recommendations.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"596c820e-21ec-4685-b435-a1fe07cb2330","uuid":"dfd907bc-c7bd-4b59-86e4-2bf60fa70179","timestamp":"2026-05-15T12:45:36.469Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"EMNLP 2025 reviewer guidelines review form scoring criteria","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01Bkeh3Qn3p1rJ2y1kscEveL","content":[{"title":"NAACL-HLT 2021 Instructions for Reviewers - EMNLP 2025","url":"https://2025.emnlp.org/reviewer/instructions/"},{"title":"Changes to reviewer volunteering requirement and incentives in May 2025 cycle (EMNLP 2025)","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/incentives2025"},{"title":"Automatically Measuring Peer Review's Utility for Authors","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2025.emnlp-main.1476.pdf"},{"title":"ICML 2025 Peer Review FAQ","url":"https://icml.cc/Conferences/2025/PeerReviewFAQ"},{"title":"‭ACL Peer Review Committee Report‬","url":"https://www.aclweb.org/adminwiki/images/d/d3/ACL_Peer_Review_Committee_Report2_Incentives_May_2025.pdf"},{"title":"[Policy Spotlight] EMNLP 2025 Criteria for “Highly Irresponsible” Reviewers — What It Means & Why It Matters | CSPaper Forum","url":"https://forum.cspaper.org/topic/70/policy-spotlight-emnlp-2025-criteria-for-highly-irresponsible-reviewers-what-it-means-why-it-matters"},{"title":"[Policy Spotlight] EMNLP 2025 Criteria for “Highly Irresponsible” Reviewers — What It Means & Why It Matters | CSPaper","url":"https://cspaper.org/topic/70/policy-spotlight-emnlp-2025-criteria-for-highly-irresponsible-reviewers-what-it-means-why-it-matters"},{"title":"EMNLP 2025 Conference | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=EMNLP%2F2025%2FConference"},{"title":"ACL Policies for Review and Citation - Admin Wiki","url":"https://www.aclweb.org/adminwiki/index.php/ACL_Policies_for_Review_and_Citation"},{"title":"Authors Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/authors"}]},"Based on the search results, here's what I found about EMNLP 2025 reviewer guidelines and scoring criteria:\n\n## Scoring Scale\n\nEMNLP 2025 uses a 5-point scale with half-point increments, similar to ACL 2020. The detailed explanation for each point level is provided in the review form.\n\nImportantly, a rating of 3 (ambivalent) is allowed, and reviewers are encouraged to take a stand on whether the paper is above or below the borderline by selecting 2.5 or 3.5, though if a paper is truly borderline or the reviewer cannot decide, a score of 3 should be used.\n\n## Review Form Structure\n\nThe review form consists of four main sections, with the first being an In-Depth Review section for providing overall assessment of the paper, which includes a core review that should describe the main contributions the paper intended to make and how well it succeeds.\n\n## Reproducibility Assessment\n\nEMNLP 2025 includes a reproducibility checklist, and reviewers answer questions about the paper's reproducibility using scores of 1-5. An \"N/A\" score may be used for papers that do not include empirical results.\n\n## Decision-Making Process\n\nDecisions are made not just on scores and certainly not on average scores, but also take into account the whole review, reviewer discussion, and Area Chair meta-reviews and recommendations."],"durationSeconds":6.87515416}}
